<title>USA: International Imaging board ends buyback.</title>
<headline>International Imaging board ends buyback.</headline>
<dateline>AMHERST, N.Y. 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Imaging Materials Inc said Tuesday that its board of directors had ended its common stock repurchase plan.</p>
<p>The company had announced in April that it would buy back 500,000 shares. but earlier this month PAXAR Corp said it had signed a definitive pact to buy International Imaging for $200 million, or $24 a share.</p>
</text>
